        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-ink leading-tight mb-5">Anxiety and Depression: How to Find a Psychologist in North Cyprus</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">Finding a psychologist is hard enough. Finding one who speaks your language, understands your background, and offers a style that works for you — in a small territory like North Cyprus — can feel genuinely daunting. This guide cuts through the noise.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose-custom space-y-8">

          <div>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">The TRNC has a small but growing private therapy sector. Most reputable practitioners are based in Nicosia (Lefkoşa) or Famagusta (Gazimağusa), with a handful offering online sessions across the island. The challenge is knowing what to look for — and what to avoid.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Why finding a psychologist in North Cyprus feels harder than it should</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Several factors make this search more complicated than it would be in the UK, US or most of Europe:</p>
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Limited English-language options</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Many psychologists in TRNC work exclusively in Turkish. For expats, international students and anyone more comfortable expressing themselves in English, the pool of practitioners shrinks considerably.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Inconsistent regulation</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Psychotherapy is not as tightly regulated in TRNC as it is in the UK or EU. Titles like "psychologist" and "counsellor" can be used loosely. Knowing what credentials to look for protects you from ineffective or even harmful practice.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Stigma and privacy concerns</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">North Cyprus is a small community. Some people worry about being seen entering a therapy centre, or about their psychologist knowing their family. These concerns are valid — and they are one reason online therapy has become so popular here.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">You don't need a diagnosis to start therapy</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Therapy is not reserved for people with a clinical diagnosis. Persistent low mood, relationship difficulties, work stress, grief, identity questions, or simply feeling "stuck" are all legitimate and common reasons to start. You do not need to be in crisis.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">What to look for in a psychologist</h2>
            <ul class="space-y-4">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Relevant qualifications</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Look for a degree in psychology (BSc or MSc minimum) or a recognised counselling qualification. Ask where they trained and whether they have supervision. A good psychologist welcomes these questions.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Evidence-based approach</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Ask whether they use CBT (Cognitive Behavioural Therapy), ACT, psychodynamic therapy or EMDR. These are approaches with strong research backing for anxiety and depression. Be cautious of vague answers about "holistic" or unnamed methods.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">English fluency (if needed)</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Therapy in a second language is genuinely harder. Subtle emotions, idioms and nuance matter enormously. If English is your working language, insist on a native or highly fluent speaker.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Clear confidentiality policy</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Before starting, ask explicitly: what is shared, with whom, under what circumstances? A professional psychologist will have a clear, written confidentiality agreement ready for you.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">English-speaking therapy in Famagusta</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Mağusa Psikoloji Centre offers individual therapy in English and Turkish in Famagusta. We work with anxiety, depression, trauma, relationship difficulties and general wellbeing — for individuals of all backgrounds living in or around North Cyprus.</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">What we offer</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Individual therapy in English</li>
                  <li>• CBT, ACT and EMDR approaches</li>
                  <li>• Anxiety, depression, trauma, grief</li>
                  <li>• Online and in-person sessions</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Who we work with</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Expats and long-term residents</li>
                  <li>• International university students</li>
                  <li>• Professionals and academics</li>
                  <li>• Couples (English or Turkish)</li>
                  <li>• Anyone in North Cyprus</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">How to know if a psychologist is right for you</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The single strongest predictor of therapy success is the quality of the therapeutic relationship — not the specific technique. Use the first one or two sessions to assess this honestly.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Ask yourself after the first session:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-2">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Did I feel heard, not judged?</p>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Did the psychologist explain their approach and check what I was looking for?</p>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Did they clarify confidentiality clearly?</p>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Do I feel, even cautiously, that I could open up to this person over time?</p>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">If the answer to these is mostly yes, you have found a good starting point. If not, it is perfectly normal — and encouraged — to try another psychologist.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-accent/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-accent/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">Your first session checklist</p>
            <ul class="text-sm text-ink-muted space-y-2 mt-2">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Bring a rough sense of what you want to work on — it doesn't need to be precise</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Ask about their training, approach and experience with your specific concerns</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Confirm the confidentiality agreement before sharing anything sensitive</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Ask about cancellation policy, session frequency and how progress is reviewed</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Trust your gut — comfort and safety matter more than any credential</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
